<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali al-Mandri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali al-Mandri was a military leader from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> who refounded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetouan">Tetouan</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> around 1484, with Wattasid permission, rebuilding the ruined town with Andalusi refugees as a base against the Portuguese at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a>. His family ruled it for decades, and his daughter-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayyida-al-hurra">Sayyida al-Hurra</a> later governed the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-al-mandri.jpg" alt="Ali al-Mandri" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ideophagous · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%B6%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%AD_%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%AF%D9%8A_%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%8A_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%86%D8%B8%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%8C_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%82%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A5%D8%B3%D9%84%D8%A7%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A9%D8%8C_%D9%83%D9%88%D9%86%D9%81%D9%8A%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B4%D8%BA%D9%84_%D8%A8%D8%AA%D8%B7%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%86_5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
